WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.198 --> 00:00:03.448
(delicate piano music)

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:06.530
- [Narrator] In the
Indian state of Manipur

00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:08.973
you will find Keibul Lamjao National Park-

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:13.190
the world's only floating
wildlife sanctuary.

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:16.723
(moving piano music)

00:00:16.723 --> 00:00:19.720
Keibul Lamjao comprises
over 15 square miles

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:23.590
of rich, biodiverse wetlands,
and includes Loktak Lake,

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:26.113
the largest freshwater
lake in northern India.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:30.440
The park is known for
patches and rings of biomass

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:33.090
that float on the surface of the wetlands.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:35.470
The floating vegetation, called phumdis,

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:37.810
thrives in the park, creating a home

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:39.836
for humans and animals alike.

00:00:39.836 --> 00:00:43.336
(moving orchestral music)

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:49.850
The endangered sangai, a
subspecies of brow-antlered deer,

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:51.980
are only found in the park.

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:53.870
They have been called the binding soul

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:55.293
between humans and nature.

00:00:56.290 --> 00:00:58.510
The sangai was believed
to be nearing extinction

00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:02.160
in the 1950s, but thanks to
aggressive conservation efforts

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.963
their numbers have steadily
increased to more than 200.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:09.130
Still relatively unknown
outside the region,

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:11.670
Keibul Lamjao National Park is truly

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:13.515
one of India's hidden gems.

00:01:13.515 --> 00:01:16.765
(delicate piano music)

